{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_reads.py","reason":"The guard at the single _tracker() chokepoint all seven library read entries funnel through, mirroring the write path _ensure_initialized"},{"path":"src/rebar/_errors.py","reason":"Add store_uninitialized to KNOWN_ERROR_CODES so the fault is machine-readable over the MCP envelope instead of requiring message-text matching (code review api-compat finding)"},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/server.py","reason":"The one caller that legitimately depended on the old degrade-to-empty: the read-only audit web index must render empty rather than 500, scoped to the store_uninitialized code (code review finding)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py","reason":"Regression coverage: every guarded read raises, initialized-but-empty still returns [], read/write parity, audit index degrades, non-store failures still propagate"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_e4_init.py","reason":"Update the expectation that asserted reads return [] without init, keeping the no-silent-creation invariant the file exists to protect"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_mcp_error_envelope_heldout.py","reason":"Pin the cross-interface library arm to the fixture store via the file own _pin helper; it was never scoped, and passed only because a missing store also yielded ticket_not_found"},{"path":"tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json","reason":"Record the intended public-surface change (the new error code) via the sanctioned gen_api_surface.py --update"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"Document the behavior change and the migration path for callers that relied on the empty-list degrade"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787727394300681001,"uuid":"6a16230c-af41-480e-91ce-e832d028fe9e"}